{title: Draw Near}
{artist: Jaye Thomas}
{key: C}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C] Bowed before the throne of [Am]grace [F]again
[C] Come reveal Yourself to [Am]us   [F]
[C] All that matters is that [Am]You are [F]pleased
[C] With the song that we lift [Am]up   [F]

{comment: Pre-chorus}
With hearts wide [G]open we [Am]sing our [Dm]song to You
With [G]expectation we [Am]ask in [F]faith

{comment: Chorus}
Draw [C]near to us, O [F/C]God
As we draw [G/C]near, as we come close to Your [F/C]heart
(Close to Your [C]heart)

{comment: Verse 2}
[C] You’re our deepest heart’s [Am]desire  [F]
[C] Come and meet us where we [Am]are  [F]
[C] Find here that which You are [Am]drawn [F]to
[C] A broken and a contrite [Am]heart [F]

{comment: Interlude}
[G]  /  [Am]  /  [F]  /  /  /  [G]  /  [Am]  /  [Dm]  /  /  /

{comment: Bridge}
[C] We came here to meet with You  [Dm]
[Am] We won’t leave until we do  [F]

{comment: Bridge 2}
[C] We climb this [Dm]mountain
[Am] To pull back the [F]curtain
[C] We’re desperately [Dm]crying
[Am] Show us Your [F]glory
